# Locram-new backend rules

These are the rules the user stated for this rewrite. Follow them. Do not add ceremony that is not here.

This file overrides the user-level feature-folder package rule. In this project, layers own folders and features are modules.

## Goal

- Keep the product as functional as it is now.
- Significantly reduce the quantity of code.
- Improve readability.
- Locram does not need complex code. Prefer the easy version.
- Keep the architectural foundation: repositories, models, schemas, services, abstractions.
- Build in a new empty project (`locram-new`). Do not strangler-refactor the old repo.
- Feature by feature. Nothing redundant.
- No pull requests until the rewrite is finished.
- Do not commit unless the user asks after reviewing the work.
- Do not restore `lint_src_architecture.py`.

## What must not exist

- No `di/` package.
- No `Runtime`.
- No `Context`.
- No containers.
- No `make_runtime`.
- No controllers.
- No presenters.
- No extra API layers.
- No stdlib HTTP server. Use FastAPI.
- No `/views`.
- No inner packages under a feature when one module is enough.
- No `isinstance`.
- No errors stored as variables.
- No `dict[str, object]`.
- No `Any` unless the value is truly any.
- No `_require_*` helpers.
- No detached module-level SQL or helper blobs when they belong on a class or in the caller.
- No abbreviations in names we invent.

```python
# ❌
pages_service = (
    context.pages
    if context is not None and context.pages is not None
    else self._runtime.pages
)
```

## Dependency tree

- `dependencies.py` has getters only: `get_engine`, `get_session`, `get_db`, `get_<feature>_repository`, `get_<feature>_service`.
- Engine and session factory live in `database.py`.
- `get_db` yields one sync `Session` per request. Repositories take that session.
- FastAPI uses `Depends(get_db)`. MCP has no request scope, so a tool-module `get_<feature>_service()` opens `get_session()` and reuses the same repository getters.
- Repositories inherit `BaseRepository` and `I<Feature>Repository`.
- Every class dependency is an `__init__` argument, typed as the interface.
- If `PageService` needs a page repository, it takes `page_repository: IPageRepository` in `__init__`.
- Name every interface `I<Class>`: `IPageService`, `IPageRepository`.
- Exactly one repository and one service per feature.
- Skip the SQL model and Alembic revision when the feature is not stored in SQLite. Attachments are files under `attachments_path`. Smart-folder presets are JSON under `filter_presets_path`.
- Exactly one implementation per service or repository unless the business logic literally needs more than one.
- As many service modules as features. Prefer `/services` with `pages.py`, not `/services/pages/page_service.py`.
- Prefer one module inside a package. Very few exceptions.

```python
# ✅
class PageService(IPageService):
    def __init__(self, page_repository: IPageRepository) -> None:
        self._page_repository = page_repository
```

## Folder layout

Backend code lives under `backend/src/`. Layer folders, feature modules:

```text
src/
  models/<feature>.py
  schemas/<feature>.py
  exceptions/<feature>.py
  interfaces/repositories/<feature>.py
  interfaces/services/<feature>.py
  repositories/<feature>.py
  services/<feature>.py
  api/main.py
  api/<feature>.py
  mcp_server/main.py
  mcp_server/protocol.py
  mcp_server/<feature>.py
  database.py
  dependencies.py
```

- `models/` contains only the SQLAlchemy model.
- Enums and Pydantic shapes live in `schemas/`.
- Exceptions live in `exceptions/`.
- Use SQLAlchemy for SQLite models.
- Do not mix exceptions, schemas, or utils into the model file.
- Schema changes go through Alembic. Repositories do not create tables, sessions, or run `initialize`.
- Import models in `alembic/env.py` so metadata is complete.

## Transports

- `/api` and `/mcp`. Both have `main.py`.
- `api/main.py` defines the uvicorn application.
- `mcp_server/main.py` defines the MCP server.
- Feature modules in `/api` are routes.
- Feature modules in `/mcp_server` are tools.
- `mcp_server/protocol.py` holds `MCPServerApp`. Do not put that protocol in a feature module.
- Do not use `@mcp.tool`. `main.py` imports `pages as pages_tools` and `links as link_tools`, then calls `register(mcp_server)`.
- MCP is a foundation of the project. Do not skip it.
- Do not add a CLI unless asked.
- The official Python package `mcp` is the SDK. Our tools package is `mcp_server`.
- Routes type the service as `page_service: IPageService = Depends(get_page_service)`.
- The exception handler lives in `api/main.py`, not as a helper in a route module.
- Never construct a repository or service inside a route or a tool.

## Types and mypy

- Everything is typed so `mypy --strict .` passes.
- Run `mypy --strict .` from `backend/`.
- Banned: adapting mypy config to stub or disable errors. Fix the code.
- Types come from typed functions, returns, and variables. Do not check types at runtime.
- Remove as many if-else branches and defensive statements as possible.
- Serialize an ORM `Page` to `PageRecord` before `apply`. `apply` does not take the SQLAlchemy model.

```python
# ✅
record = payload.apply(PageRecord.model_validate(page))
page.title = record.title

# ❌
payload.apply(page)
```

- Do not write `payload.title if payload.title is not None else current.title` chains. Use one simple apply (`model_dump(exclude_unset=True)` / `model_copy`).

## Errors

- Raise exceptions. Do not return error dicts.
- Do not keep errors as variables.
- Every custom exception inherits `AppError`.
- `api/main.py` has one exception handler for `AppError`. Do not add a handler per feature.
- Callers that need a page write this, every time:

```python
page = self._page_repository.get(page_id)

if page is None:
    raise PageNotFoundError(page_id)
```

## Docstrings

- Each service interface (`interfaces/services/<feature>.py`) has one class docstring that describes the service, and therefore the feature.
- Do not add docstrings anywhere else.

## Helpers

- Minimize detached helper functions.
- Title heading is a small method on the page service, defined at the caller, not a shared monster util.
- A method that does not use `self` is `@staticmethod`.
- SQL statements and similar blobs live inside the class that uses them, not at module top level.

## Naming and spacing

- Never write abbreviations. Use full words (`pages_search_index`, not `FTS` / `pages_fts`). Keep a vendor name only when it is the engine's name (`USING fts5`).
- NEVER write collapsed code with no vertical spacing. Blank lines between steps, around conditionals, and before `return`.

```python
# ✅
page = self._page_repository.get(page_id)

if page is None:
    raise PageNotFoundError(page_id)

return self._to_detail(page)

# ❌
page = self._page_repository.get(page_id)
if page is None: raise PageNotFoundError(page_id)
return self._to_detail(page)
```

## Frontend

- Everything we build is for desktop. Ship the desktop HTTP/MCP contract with the feature, not later.
- Prefer the existing desktop code.
- Frontend may stay messy. Clean it later if asked.
- Backend must be clean. Do not copy old backend ceremony into locram-new.
- Desktop page/link/search calls send `?base_ref=local:<entry_id>`. Resolve that file. `read` blocks writes. Implicit writes fail when more than one writable local base exists.
- Desktop freshness is `GET /api/data-version` (`{ item: { version, updated_at } }`) and `GET /api/events` SSE `data-version`.
- Desktop embedding settings are `/api/desktop/embedding-settings` plus `/validate`, `/bootstrap`, and `POST /api/desktop/embeddings/run`. Never return the Hugging Face key.

## Checks

After backend edits, from `backend/`:

```text
mypy --strict .
ruff check . --fix
```

## Feature order

- Pages first. A page lives in one SQLite file. Bases only choose which file later.
- Bridge is HTTP only: `GET /api/health` and `GET /api/runtime`. No MCP tools.
- Attachments are files under `attachments_path`, referenced from page content as `![[filename]]`.
- Smart folders are JSON presets plus eight built-in scopes. Pages embed filters; matching is metadata-only.
- Embeddings store float32 vectors on the page SQLite file. Hybrid search fuses FTS with cosine similarity and falls back to FTS when no provider is configured. Settings choose hosted, Hugging Face, or Ollama. Hosted uses the enrolled Access relay token against `embed.locram.app`, or a bootstrap token before enroll.
- Changes are SQLite triggers on pages/links. Do not inject a change service into page or link writes.
- Backups are SQLite snapshot files next to the knowledge file (`<db-parent>/backups/locram-<trigger>-<timestamp>.db`). No SQL model. Restore writes `pre_restore` first.
- Exports are scoped SQLite artifacts next to the knowledge file (`<db-parent>/exports/locram-export-<timestamp>.db`). No SQL model. Inspect any locram SQLite path.
- Merges are additive. Plan first. Same-id same-content is skipped; same-id different content is blocked. Execute writes a pre_merge backup first. No operation-log or provenance tables.
- Sharing stores local owner grants on host-state. Invite minting signs with Access credentials. Accepted shares persist locally and appear as `shared:` working bases. `managed:ggl` and `managed:documentation` are built-in snapshot bases. Refresh copies packaged seeds into `managed-bases/`.
- Access is the device client for the existing Cloudflare broker (`https://broker.locram.app`). Enrollment, identity, in-process websocket relay, pending authorizations, connected sessions, and share-session resolve live here. Public status is `preferences/access.json`; secrets are a sibling file and never appear in API responses. Hosted embeddings use the enrolled relay token. Invite minting and `shared:` / `managed:` working bases use the same enrollment.
- Do not start the next feature unless asked.
